# Corpus fixtures are byte-exact test data: manifest.toml records a sha256 for
# every one of them, so any end-of-line translation on checkout is a
# provenance failure, not a formatting detail.
#
# This is not hypothetical. custom_encoding.pdf and huge_page_count.pdf are
# hand-authored by generate_synthetic.py and contain no NUL byte, so git
# classifies them as text and a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the
# GitHub runner default) rewrites their LF to CRLF -- which is exactly how the
# hash check first failed on the windows-latest leg of the CI matrix.
files/** binary
